            "id": "pc4_s1_c4",
            "chapterNum": 4,
            "title": "1. Fundamental Rules & Supplementary Rules (Part I): (d) Retirement",
            "content": "### Tier 1: Syllabus Anchor & Statutory Codal Authority\n- **Prescribed Authority**: Fundamental Rules (FR 56) & CCS (Pension) Rules\n- **Relevant Codal Provisions**: FR 56(a) (Superannuation age 60), FR 56(j) (Compulsory retirement in public interest), FR 56(k) (Voluntary retirement after 30 years/50-55 age), FR 56(m)\n- **CAG Examination Relevance**: Tests statutory compliance, verification criteria, and practical audit drafting.\n\n### Tier 2: Statutory Provisions, Definitions & Prescribed Thresholds\n• **Retirement Age**: Last day of month in which official attains **60 years** (if DOB is 1st of month, retires on last day of preceding month).\n• **FR 56(j) Notice**: 3 months' notice or 3 months' pay and allowances in lieu of notice; applicable at age 50 (Group A/B entering before age 35) or age 55 (others).\n• **Voluntary Retirement (FR 56(k))**: Minimum **3 months' written notice** to Appointing Authority.\n\n### Tier 3: Practical Accounting, Procedures & Official Codal Forms\n• **Superannuation Notice Form**, Form 5 (Pension Application), 3 Months' Pay in Lieu Order.\n\n### Tier 4: Statutory Exceptions, Restrictions & Competent Authorities\n• Extension in service beyond 60 years is prohibited except for Cabinet Secretary, Home/Defence/Foreign Secretaries, and exceptional scientists under FR 56(d).\n\n### Tier 5: SAS Examination Case Studies, Practical Calculations & Half-Margins\n• **Practical Case Problem**: An employee born on 01-07-1964 reaches superannuation. Determine exact date of retirement.\n• **Codal Rule & Answer**: FR 56(a) Proviso: An employee born on the 1st of a month retires on the *afternoon of the last day of the preceding month* = 30-06-2024 (NOT 31-07-2024).\n\n---\n### Comprehensive Codal Study Notes & Statutory Analysis\n### Fundamental Rules (FR) Part-I: Retirement under FR 56 (Superannuation, FR 56(j) & Voluntary Retirement)\n\n#### 1. Statutory Provisions Governing Retirement\nThe retirement of civil government servants is governed by **Fundamental Rule 56 (FR 56)** and the Central Civil Services (Pension) Rules:\n- **FR 56(a) - Age of Compulsory Superannuation**:\n  - Every government servant retires compulsorily from service on the afternoon of the last day of the month in which they attain the **age of 60 years**.\n  - *Exception*: A government servant whose date of birth is the **first of a month** shall retire from service on the afternoon of the **last day of the preceding month** on attaining the age of 60 years (e.g. Born on 1st July $\\rightarrow$ Retires on 30th June).\n\n#### 2. Compulsory Retirement in Public Interest: FR 56(j) & FR 56(l)\nUnder Fundamental Rule 56(j), the appropriate authority possesses the absolute statutory power to retire any government servant in the public interest by giving **three months' notice in writing** or three months' pay and allowances in lieu of notice:\n- **Applicability Criteria**:\n  - *Group A and Group B Officers*: If they entered service before attaining the age of 35 years, upon attaining the **age of 50 years**. In all other cases, upon attaining the **age of 55 years**.\n  - *Group C Personnel*: Who are not governed by any pension rules, upon completing **30 years of qualifying service**.\n- **Nature of FR 56(j)**:\n  - Not a penal measure; does not amount to dismissal or removal under Article 311 of the Constitution.\n  - Entitled to full admissible pension and gratuity earned up to the date of retirement.\n  - Used to weed out deadwood, corrupt officials, and personnel with compromised integrity or persistent inefficiency based on comprehensive review of Annual Performance Appraisal Reports (APAR).\n\n#### 3. Voluntary Retirement under FR 56(k) & Rule 43 of Pension Rules\n- A government servant may voluntarily retire from service after completing **20 years of qualifying service** (under Rule 43 of CCS Pension Rules) or upon attaining the age of 50/55 years (under FR 56(k)).\n- Requires **three months' notice in writing** to the appointing authority.\n- Notice of voluntary retirement cannot be withdrawn except with the specific approval of the appointing authority, applied before the intended date of retirement.",
            "gist": "FR 56 superannuation at 60 years. FR 56(j) allows compulsory retirement in public interest at age 50/55 with 3 months' notice. Voluntary retirement allowed after 20/30 years service.",
            "crux": "1. Superannuation age is 60 years (last day of the month).\n2. FR 56(j) compulsory retirement requires 3 months notice or pay in lieu.\n3. Voluntary retirement requires 3 months written notice.",
