            "id": "pc4_s1_c8",
            "chapterNum": 8,
            "title": "4. Central Civil Services (Joining Time) Rules",
            "content": "### Tier 1: Syllabus Anchor & Statutory Codal Authority\n- **Prescribed Authority**: Central Civil Services (Joining Time) Rules, 1979\n- **Relevant Codal Provisions**: Rules 4 (Admissibility), 5 (Calculation of Joining Time), 6 (Combination with leave)\n- **CAG Examination Relevance**: Tests statutory compliance, verification criteria, and practical audit drafting.\n\n### Tier 2: Statutory Provisions, Definitions & Prescribed Thresholds\n• **Distance Slabs for Joining Time**:\n  - Same station or distance $\\le 8$ km: **1 day**.\n  - Distance $> 8$ km and $\\le 1,000$ km: **10 days**.\n  - Distance $> 1,000$ km and $\\le 2,000$ km: **12 days** (15 days if air travel authorized).\n  - Distance $> 2,000$ km: **15 days**.\n• **Crediting Unutilized Joining Time**: Unavailed joining time credited to Earned Leave account subject to 300 days accumulation ceiling.\n\n### Tier 3: Practical Accounting, Procedures & Official Codal Forms\n• **Joining Time Order**, Transfer Notification, Relief Memo, Service Book Entry.\n\n### Tier 4: Statutory Exceptions, Restrictions & Competent Authorities\n• No joining time is admissible in cases of temporary transfer not exceeding 180 days or transfer at own request.\n\n### Tier 5: SAS Examination Case Studies, Practical Calculations & Half-Margins\n• **SAS Problem**: Official transferred from Delhi to Kolkata (1,450 km) at own request. DDO granted 12 days joining time with full pay.\n• **Audit Objection**: Violation of Rule 4(4); transfer at own request attracts zero joining time and zero transfer TA.\n\n---\n### Comprehensive Codal Study Notes & Statutory Analysis\n### Central Civil Services (Joining Time) Rules, 1979: Provisions, Calculations & Unavailed Credit\n\n#### 1. Statutory Scope & Applicability\nThe **CCS (Joining Time) Rules, 1979** govern the transit period granted to a government servant upon transfer from one official station to another in the public interest.\n- **When Admissible**: Admissible only on transfers made in the **public interest**. Transfers made at the employee's own request carry **no joining time**.\n\n#### 2. Scale of Joining Time Admissible\nJoining time is calculated based on the distance between the old headquarters and new headquarters:\n```\n+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                        JOINING TIME ENTITLEMENT MATRIX                            |\n+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| DISTANCE BETWEEN OLD & NEW STATION    | JOINING TIME ADMISSIBLE                   |\n| 1. Within same station / no change    | 1 Day only (joining in next morning)      |\n|    of residence                       |                                           |\n| 2. Distance <= 1,000 km               | 10 Days                                   |\n| 3. Distance > 1,000 km and <= 2,000 km| 12 Days                                   |\n| 4. Distance > 2,000 km                | 15 Days (except air travel: 12 days)      |\n| 5. Travel by Air (any distance)       | 12 Days maximum                           |\n+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```\n- *Reckoning of Distance*: Measured based on the shortest route by which the journey can ordinarily be performed.\n- *Commencement*: Joining time commences from the date of relinquishment of charge of the old post if handed over in the forenoon, or from the following day if handed over in the afternoon.\n\n#### 3. Unavailed Joining Time Credited to Earned Leave (Rule 6(1))\n- If a government servant joins the new post without utilizing the full admissible joining time (e.g., joins after 3 days instead of 12 days), the unavailed portion of joining time (9 days) is **credited to their Earned Leave (EL) account**.\n- *Ceiling*: The credit of unavailed joining time is subject to the overall statutory accumulation ceiling of **300 days of Earned Leave**.",
            "gist": "Joining time: 10 days (<=1000 km), 12 days (1001-2000 km), 15 days (>2000 km), and 1 day within same station. Unavailed joining time is credited to EL.",
            "crux": "1. Up to 1000 km = 10 days; 1001 to 2000 km = 12 days; >2000 km = 15 days.\n2. Unavailed joining time credited to EL account.\n3. Not admissible for temporary transfers up to 180 days.",
