            "id": "pc4_s3_c9",
            "chapterNum": 9,
            "title": "9. Book of Forms referred in CPWA Code",
            "content": "### Tier 1: Syllabus Anchor & Statutory Codal Authority\n- **Prescribed Authority**: Book of Forms referred to in CPWA Code (Central Public Works Accounts Code)\n- **Relevant Codal Provisions**: CPWA Book of Forms: Forms 1 to 95\n- **CAG Examination Relevance**: Tests statutory compliance, verification criteria, and practical audit drafting.\n\n### Tier 2: Statutory Provisions, Definitions & Prescribed Thresholds\n• **Form 23**: Measurement Book (MB) - Indispensable original record of measurements.\n• **Form 24**: First and Final Bill (single payment for completed small works).\n• **Form 26**: Running Account Bill A (advance payments without detailed measurement).\n• **Form 27**: Running Account Bill B (item-rate contracts with detailed measurements).\n• **Form 83**: Monthly Account submitted to AG.\n\n### Tier 3: Practical Accounting, Procedures & Official Codal Forms\n• **Measurement Book (Form 23)**, Running Account Bill (Form 27), Contractors' Ledger (Form 43), Cash Book (Form 1).\n\n### Tier 4: Statutory Exceptions, Restrictions & Competent Authorities\n• Loss of a Measurement Book (Form 23) must be reported immediately to Superintending Engineer and treated with same seriousness as loss of cash.\n\n### Tier 5: SAS Examination Case Studies, Practical Calculations & Half-Margins\n• **Exam Drill**: Identify appropriate CPWA bill forms for:\n  1. Final payment of a ₹25,000 whitewashing work: `Form 24`\n  2. 4th running bill for construction of a bridge: `Form 27`\n  3. Advance payment for machinery: `Form 26`\n\n---\n### Comprehensive Codal Study Notes & Statutory Analysis\n### Book of Forms Referred in CPWA Code: Key Registers, Vouchers & Standard Forms\n\n#### 1. The Statutory Standard Forms under CPWA Code\nPublic Works Accounts are compiled through standardized forms prescribed in the **Book of Forms of the Central Public Works Account Code (CPWA Code)**.\n- **Core Principle**: Standard forms ensure uniform accounting, immutable audit trails, and strict internal checks across all civil works divisions.\n\n#### 2. Master Table of Critical CPWA Standard Forms\n| Form No. | Name of Prescribed Form | Codal Purpose & Accounting Usage |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Form 21** | **Muster Roll** | The initial daily attendance and payment record for daily-rated muster roll labor employed on departmental works. Part I: Daily attendance; Part II: Details of work measured; Part III: Unpaid wages summary. |\n| **Form 23** | **Measurement Book (MB)** | The primary legal and technical record of all works executed and supplies received. Forms the sole basis for all payments to contractors. |\n| **Form 24** | **First and Final Bill** | Used for single-installment payments to contractors when the work or supply is completed in a single spell without intermediate running bills. |\n| **Form 26** | **Running Account Bill A** | Standard white bill form used for advance payments or secured advances to contractors for works in progress. |\n| **Form 27** | **Running Account Bill B** | Standard yellow bill form used for running payments to contractors where payments are made on the basis of actual detailed measurements recorded in the MB. |\n| **Form 43** | **Contractors' Ledger** | A personal ledger account maintained for every individual contractor showing all debits (payments, materials issued, recoveries) and credits (work passed). |\n| **Form 53** | **Transfer Entry Order (TEO)** | Used for transferring debits or credits from one head of account or work to another, rectifying misclassifications, and adjusting suspense items. |\n| **Form 80** | **Monthly Account (PW Divisions)** | The consolidated monthly account compiled by the Divisional Accountant and signed by the Executive Engineer, rendered to the AG (A&E) by the 10th of each month. |",
